        "Finite real complete Hilbert/Borel full space E, including dimension zero; arbitrary measurable parameter space S; actual measurable eta:S->R and y:S->E with eta(s)>0 for every s. These coordinate-free/parameter-space extensions are disclosed. Printed Lemma4.2 inherits eta>0 from Section3.1; the eta<=1 premise of neighboring Lemma4.1 is not consumed.",
        "No supplied proximal point, minimizer, measurable selector, gradient estimate, Lipschitz bound or Markov kernel. All are produced from the literal potential and actual Gaussian pushforward. The source numerical-prox call cap eta<=1/(2beta) remains a separate computational contract. Output first moment and allsigned Laplace domains, including actual mean, are also produced internally."
      ],
      "statement": "Produce a measurable exact proximal selector p satisfying p+eta*gradientV(p)=y, the genuine quantitative quadratic minimum and uniqueness, and fixed-eta nonexpansivity. The literal Gaussian gradient evaluator G(s,z)=gradientV(p(s)+sqrt(eta(s))*z) is jointly measurable and obeys input/noise Lipschitz constants 1 and sqrteta for equal eta. Produce an actual Markov kernel K(s)=stdGaussian.map(G(s,-)). This covers the exact evaluator (3.2) and only Lemma4.2 (4.4)-(4.5), with no posterior or finite-query claim. Additionally id is genuinely Bochner integrable under every K_s, and exp(t*inner(a,w-int v dK_s)) is integrable under K_s for every vector a and real signed t. This centers at the actual output mean, and proves only the necessary domain for4.3, not its sharp MGF bound.",
      "formula": "F_s(x)=V(x)+\\|x-y_s\\|^2/(2\\eta_s),\\quad p_s+\\eta_s\\nabla V(p_s)=y_s,\\quad G(s,z)=\\nabla V(p_s+\\sqrt{\\eta_s}z),\\quad K_s=G(s,\\cdot)_\\#\\gamma.\\quad m_s=\\int w\\,dK_s,\\quad\\mathrm{id}\\in L^1(K_s;E),\\quad e^{t\\langle a,w-m_s\\rangle}\\in L^1(K_s)\\ (a\\in E,t\\in\\mathbb R).",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Derive the real gradient estimates",
          "text": "Reuse the actual C2 Hessian-to-gradient and strong-convexity APIs. The source upper bound supplies gradientV Lipschitz1. The convex gradient-step theorem supplies id-gradientV Lipschitz1, and convexity supplies monotonicity. None is a theorem premise.",
          "formula": "\\operatorname{Lip}(\\nabla V)\\le1,\\quad\\operatorname{Lip}(I-\\nabla V)\\le1,\\quad\\langle\\nabla V(x)-\\nabla V(z),x-z\\rangle\\ge0.",
          "lean": "actual_gradient_bounds; QuadraticRegularization; SmoothnessEquivalences; GradientDescentContraction; StrongConvexFirstOrder"
        },
        {
          "title": "Construct the actual pointwise damped map",
          "text": "For each actual positive eta, T_s contracts with its own coefficient eta_s/(1+eta_s)<1. The coefficients may approach one over the parameter space. Banach fixed-point construction is pointwise and makes no uniform-parameter contraction or runtime assumption.",
          "formula": "T_s(x)=(1+\\eta_s)^{-1}[y_s+\\eta_s(x-\\nabla V(x))],\\quad c_s=\\eta_s/(1+\\eta_s)<1.",
          "lean": "parameterized_damped_point; ContractingWith"
        },
        {
          "title": "Obtain joint measurability from actual iterates",
          "text": "Every iterate T_s^n(0) is measurable in s from actual measurable eta/y and the continuous id-minus-gradient map. Pointwise Banach convergence with the actual c_s and measurable-limit theorem give a measurable p. Uniform convergence and an upper eta cap are unnecessary; no measurable selector is supplied.",
          "formula": "p_s=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}T_s^n(0),\\quad s\\mapsto p_s\\text{ measurable, even when }\\sup_s c_s=1.",
          "lean": "ContractingWith.fixedPoint; tendsto_iterate_fixedPoint; measurable_of_tendsto_metrizable"
