          "formula": "f_{s,a}(z)=\\langle a,G(s,z)\\rangle,\\quad\\operatorname{Lip}(f_{s,a})\\le\\|a\\|\\sqrt{\\eta_s},\\quad e^{t(f_{s,a}-\\int f_{s,a}d\\gamma)}\\in L^1(\\gamma).",
          "lean": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Probability.GaussianLipschitzExponential.integrable_and_integrable_exp_centered_of_lipschitz; abs_real_inner_le_norm; LipschitzWith.of_dist_le_mul"
        },
        {
          "title": "Identify the actual center and pull back the law",
          "text": "The Bochner pushforward identity gives m_s=int G(s,z)d gamma. Integral commutation with the continuous inner-product functional gives int f_s,a d gamma=inner(a,m_s). The integrability pushforward equivalence then yields every actual centered directional exponential under K_s. This is the output own mean; no equality with a smoothed gradient is assumed or proved.",
          "formula": "m_s=\\int w\\,dK_s=\\int G(s,z)\\,d\\gamma,\\quad\\int e^{t\\langle a,w-m_s\\rangle}\\,dK_s(w)<\\infty\\quad(a\\in E,t\\in\\mathbb R).",
          "lean": "integral_map; integral_inner; inner_sub_right; integrable_map_measure"
        }
      ],
      "lean_statement": "Produce a measurable exact proximal selector p satisfying p+eta*gradientV(p)=y, the genuine quantitative quadratic minimum and uniqueness, and fixed-eta nonexpansivity. The literal Gaussian gradient evaluator G(s,z)=gradientV(p(s)+sqrt(eta(s))*z) is jointly measurable and obeys input/noise Lipschitz constants 1 and sqrteta for equal eta. Produce an actual Markov kernel K(s)=stdGaussian.map(G(s,-)). This covers the exact evaluator (3.2) and only Lemma4.2 (4.4)-(4.5), with no posterior or finite-query claim. Additionally id is genuinely Bochner integrable under every K_s, and exp(t*inner(a,w-int v dK_s)) is integrable under K_s for every vector a and real signed t. This centers at the actual output mean, and proves only the necessary domain for4.3, not its sharp MGF bound.",
      "lean_proof": "Derive the real gradient estimates; Construct the actual pointwise damped map; Obtain joint measurability from actual iterates; Recover the exact source equation; Prove the genuine minimum and uniqueness; Keep nonexpansivity at fixed eta; Use the literal Gaussian gradient evaluator; Prove the exact input and noise constants; Realize the actual Markov kernel; Produce the actual vector first moment; Apply the canonical domain leaf to the actual direction; Identify the actual center and pull back the law",
      "astis_dependencies": [
        "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.QuadraticRegularization.strongConvexOn_and_lipschitzWith_gradient_add_quadratic",
        "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.HessianStrongConvexity.strongConvexOn_univ_of_fderiv2_lower",
