        "source": "Euclidean d-dimensional source beta1/alpha=kappa^-1 and eta>0; exact argmin and Gaussian gradient definition.",
        "lean": "Source beta=1, alpha=kappa^-1, real kappa>=1; actual C2 V with kappa^-1*normv^2 <= D2V(x)[v,v] <= normv^2 for every x,v.\nFinite real complete Hilbert/Borel full space E, including dimension zero; arbitrary measurable parameter space S; actual measurable eta:S->R and y:S->E with eta(s)>0 for every s. These coordinate-free/parameter-space extensions are disclosed. Printed Lemma4.2 inherits eta>0 from Section3.1; the eta<=1 premise of neighboring Lemma4.1 is not consumed.\nNo supplied proximal point, minimizer, measurable selector, gradient estimate, Lipschitz bound or Markov kernel. All are produced from the literal potential and actual Gaussian pushforward. The source numerical-prox call cap eta<=1/(2beta) remains a separate computational contract."
      },
      {
        "source": "Actual proximal existence/uniqueness/optimality are implicit and source uses fixed-eta nonexpansivity.",
        "lean": "The constructed pointwise damped fixed point supplies measurable selector, true equation and unique quadratic minimum internally."
      },
      {
        "source": "Gaussian estimator (3.2), only input Lipschitz (4.4) and noise Lipschitz (4.5).",
        "lean": "Produce a measurable exact proximal selector p satisfying p+eta*gradientV(p)=y, the genuine quantitative quadratic minimum and uniqueness, and fixed-eta nonexpansivity. The literal Gaussian gradient evaluator G(s,z)=gradientV(p(s)+sqrt(eta(s))*z) is jointly measurable and obeys input/noise Lipschitz constants 1 and sqrteta for equal eta. Produce an actual Markov kernel K(s)=stdGaussian.map(G(s,-)). This covers the exact evaluator (3.2) and only Lemma4.2 (4.4)-(4.5), with no posterior or finite-query claim."
      },
      {
        "source": "Separate bias/MGF, posterior standardized law, Wp, warmness, numerical implementation, both main theorems and composition.",
        "lean": "Genuine Gaussian-gradient-output first Bochner moment and every signed directional centered exponential L1, plus existing exact positive-step proximal/input/noise semantics only. Sharp centered coefficient eta*normu^2/2 in4.3, bias4.2, FIRSTW2/LSI/T2/fullLemma4.2, posterior jointkernel/higher smoothing/Picard/Wp/proxywarmness/initialization/main/work/composition remainOPEN. Domain proof is authored Fernique alternative, not Gaussian concentration constant. TV never transfers unboundedcost. Exactstatements/topology alreadysealed beforeproof; no unreviewed signature gap."
      },
      {
        "source": "Section3.1 eta>0 and Lemma4.2 have no upper eta bound; neighboring Lemma4.1 alone requires eta<=1.",
        "lean": "Allpositive eta and every other existing sealed binder/output unchanged; only genuine firstmoment and signedcentered exponentialL1 outputs added."
