  "proof_review_details": {
    "generic": "Lipschitz growth produces scalar L1 using derived Gaussian vector first moment. For arbitrary signed t, abs(t) growth and actual Fernique C>0 give a finite exponential-square dominator; L=0 and degenerate laws require no additional premise.",
    "consumer": "Actual Hessian parents produce grad/id-minus-grad Lipschitz bounds. Pointwise damped contractions build measurable p without uniform eta cap; regularized gradient zero gives exact minimum and uniqueness. Monotonicity gives fixed-eta nonexpansivity. Joint measurable G yields actual Markov pushforward K. Genuine vector first L1 and actual scalar directional Lipschitzness are produced; same-law integral_map/integral_inner identify own mean before pulling back centered domains.",
    "tests": "Nonlinear unbounded norm with negative t; zero L; dimension zero; varying/unbounded eta family and actual output moment; posterior-versus-Gaussian moment distinction reviewed in the third Test without granting additional theorem credit.",
    "reader_provenance": "All cited direct ASTIS theorem calls and selected Mathlib contract names checked against actual calls/current parent interfaces. All formula fields contain single TeX backslashes, no double-slash encoding repair required.",
    "compilation_boundary": "No new compilation performed or compilation-only acceptance inferred."
  },
